@@ -70,6 +70,10 @@ As of f6c46b59. The repository keeps no decision records and no architecture doc
 - AD-25 (inherited) Tests run with Django's runner, one `tests/` package per app; CI runs them on SQLite, PostgreSQL, MySQL and MariaDB with Python 3.12 to 3.15, plus `mypy --strict` and a coverage run; `TransactionTestCase` appears once, where a test needs real commits and an `IntegrityError`. Why: the supported-environment promises are only proven by running the suite on each of them (inferred). Evidence: `.github/workflows/tests.yml` `matrix`; `hc/api/tests/test_notify.py` `TransactionTestCase`.
 - AD-26 (inherited) Static typing is enforced: every module starts with `from __future__ import annotations` and the tree must pass `mypy --strict` with the django-stubs plugin; formatting is ruff. Why: the style section asks for ruff and simplicity, and the strict type check runs in CI on every push (stated: `CONTRIBUTING.md` "Code Style"). Evidence: `.github/workflows/mypy.yml` `mypy --strict`; `mypy.ini` `django-stubs`.
 - AD-27 (inherited) User-visible changes are written into `CHANGELOG.md` under the top "## v..." heading, and the application's displayed version is read from the first such heading at start-up. Why: the changelog is the release record and the running version is derived from it (stated: `CHANGELOG.md` "All notable changes"). Evidence: `hc/settings.py` `VERSION`; `CHANGELOG.md` "Unreleased".
+- AD-28 (inherited) A project has up to two Management API keys, read-write (`hcw_`) and read-only (`hcr_`), and two view decorators turn them into capabilities: `authorize` accepts only the read-write key (from the `X-Api-Key` header or the JSON body of a POST) and guards every endpoint that creates, updates, deletes, pauses or resumes a check as well as list integrations, list pings and ping body; `authorize_read` accepts either key from the `X-Api-Key` header only and guards list checks, get check, list status changes and list badges; a missing or wrong key is HTTP 401 with a JSON `{"error": ...}` body; with a read-only key `Check.to_dict(readonly=True)` leaves out `uuid`, `ping_url`, `update_url`, `pause_url`, `resume_url` and `channels` and adds `unique_key`. Read-write members create and revoke keys on the Project Settings page, and a new key is shown once. Why: a script that only reports status can hold a key that can neither change a check nor learn how to ping it, and naming the decorator on each route makes the choice visible (stated: `templates/docs/api.md` "Omits sensitive information from the API responses"). Evidence: `hc/api/decorators.py` `authorize_read`; `hc/api/decorators.py` `authorize`; `hc/api/models.py` `to_dict`; `hc/accounts/views.py` `project`; consumers `templates/front/dashboard.html` and `hc/integrations/prometheus/views.py` `metrics`.
+- AD-29 (inherited) The status a caller sees is derived when it is read: `Check.get_status` combines the stored status, last ping, schedule or timeout, grace time and the clock into `new`, `up`, `grace`, `down` or `paused`, and the Management API, badges, Prometheus view and web UI report that value rather than the stored column. Why: a ping request updates the stored status at once, but the stored `down` is written later by the alert process (AD-4), so the column alone would show an overdue check as up (stated: `hc/api/models.py` `get_status` "Return current status for display"). Evidence: `hc/api/models.py` `get_status`; `hc/api/models.py` `to_dict`; `hc/api/views.py` `badge`; `hc/integrations/prometheus/views.py` `metrics`.
+- AD-30 (inherited) Management API views are CSRF-exempt and open to browsers on other origins: the `cors` decorator answers `OPTIONS` with 204, answers methods outside the view's list with 405, and adds `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` and `Access-Control-Allow-Headers: X-Api-Key` to every response. Why: the credential is a header that a browser never attaches by itself, so no cookie or session is exposed and a page on another site can act only if it already holds the key (inferred). Evidence: `hc/api/decorators.py` `cors`; `hc/api/views.py` `checks`; `hc/api/tests/test_list_checks.py` `test_it_handles_options`.
+- AD-31 (accepted) The API that external dashboards use to list a project's checks with their status and last ping time is the existing list call `GET /api/v3/checks/` with the project's read-only key (AD-28); no endpoint, key or token type, table, column, migration, setting, dependency, process, response format or URL prefix is added, and the repository change is limited to tests in `hc/api/tests` that pin what the request relies on. Why: the call already returns each check's `status` and `last_ping` as JSON, the read-only key is already refused by every state-changing route, and the bundled `/tv/` dashboard and the Prometheus scrape already consume it; a second surface would have to copy and then keep in step the key rules, serialization, status derivation and CORS handling. Alternatives: a dedicated status-only endpoint with its own serializer; a new scoped token model with its own table and migration; the JSON badge (counts per tag only, no per-check list or last ping time) or the Prometheus text endpoint (not JSON, no last ping time). Basis: S1.
 
